1. e4 e6 2. d4 c5 3. d5 { Pushes past the c5 pawn and gains space. The pawn on d5 cramps Black's pieces and cannot easily be attacked. }
3... exd5 ( 3... Nf6 4. Nc3 { Develops and protects the e4 pawn, which Black's knight attacks. } 4... d6 ( 4... exd5? 5. e5! { Hits the knight, which has no good square, and Black's d5 pawn will fall. } 5... Ng8 6. Qxd5 ) 5. dxe6 { Takes the pawn so Black cannot keep the closed centre it wants. } 5... Bxe6 6. Nge2 )
4. exd5 d6 5. Nc3 { Develops and guards d5. The open e-file is what Black needs to fight for. }
5... Nf6 6. Bd3 { The bishop eyes the kingside and protects the pawn on e4 if needed. }
6... Be7 7. Nge2 { Develops without blocking the f-pawn and heads for g3. }
7... O-O 8. O-O { Plan: finish castling, bring the knight to g3 and play a4 and Bf4. Black's bishop on c8 has few good squares, and ours is free. } *
